# markdown-syntax AST->HTML conformance suite v1: syntax decisions
source: literal_autolinks
decision: Literal autolinks are part of the syntax, also inside text a CommonMark `<…>` leaves as text.
count: 15

--- case 1 options allow_dangerous_html,allow_dangerous_protocol label-bytes 66 input-bytes 24 expected-bytes 70
from commonmark/autolink.cases #11; verified: cmark-gfm, micromark
--- input
<http://foo.bar/baz bim>
--- expected
<p>&lt;<a href="http://foo.bar/baz">http://foo.bar/baz</a> bim&gt;</p>
--- end
